{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463348",
      "title": "Adding a Battle Log",
      "lectureOrder": 59,
      "videoOrder": 53,
      "sourceHash": "631d0574be99ee2ed181b254a6d7d9f38717c545efc9c3ea3729f434adeed6fd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.01,
          "en": "So let's move on to the battle log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.01,
          "end": 6.65,
          "en": "And there are certainly many ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.65,
          "end": 8.84,
          "en": "of implementing such a log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.84,
          "end": 11.759,
          "en": "I want to have a log where we can add messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.759,
          "end": 16.11,
          "en": "that basically keep track of which action occurred?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.11,
          "end": 18.67,
          "en": "And who started this action?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.67,
          "end": 22.04,
          "en": "And which value was connected to this action?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.04,
          "end": 24.74,
          "en": "For example, how much damage was dealt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.74,
          "end": 27.21,
          "en": "For that we should go back to app.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.21,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "and add a new method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 31.99,
          "en": "which could be called addLogMessage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.99,
          "end": 34.42,
          "en": "because that's what we're going to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.42,
          "end": 38.76,
          "en": "This method should take three parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 42.113,
          "en": "It should take the information, who did something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.36,
          "end": 45.58,
          "en": "So I'm going to name it who.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.58,
          "end": 48.16,
          "en": "Then I want to know what happened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.16,
          "end": 51.21,
          "en": "Did we attack? Did we heal?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.21,
          "end": 54.18,
          "en": "So I'm going to add a what here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.18,
          "end": 58.11,
          "en": "and I need to know the value, how much damage was dealt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 59.92,
          "en": "How much did we heal for?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.92,
          "end": 62.36,
          "en": "So these are the free parameters we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.36,
          "end": 64.96,
          "en": "Who, what and value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.96,
          "end": 66.43,
          "en": "And with this information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.43,
          "end": 68.85,
          "en": "I want to add a new log message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.85,
          "end": 71.8,
          "en": "to a growing list of logMessages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.8,
          "end": 74.3,
          "en": "which then can be output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.3,
          "end": 77.38,
          "en": "in this battle log on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.38,
          "end": 80.46000000000001,
          "en": "Hence, what we need a data property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.46000000000001,
          "end": 82.62,
          "en": "an array of logMessages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.62,
          "end": 85.89,
          "en": "which can change and which Vue tracks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.89,
          "end": 87.39,
          "en": "to be aware of changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 91,
          "en": "so that it updates the UI when it changed?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91,
          "end": 95.64,
          "en": "So therefore here, I'm going to add a logMessages array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.64,
          "end": 97.96000000000001,
          "en": "which is empty initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.96000000000001,
          "end": 99.57,
          "en": "And whilst we're at it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 102.7,
          "en": "we can also already reset it to an empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.7,
          "end": 104.35,
          "en": "when we start a new game.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.35,
          "end": 107.563,
          "en": "So set logMessages back to an empty array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.42,
          "end": 112.894,
          "en": "but now that we got logMessages in addLogMessage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.894,
          "end": 116.64,
          "en": "I want to add a new log message to this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.64,
          "end": 118.91,
          "en": "whenever this method is called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.91,
          "end": 121.86,
          "en": "And I want to add it at the beginning of the array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.86,
          "end": 125.56,
          "en": "so that the latest message is always right on top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.56,
          "end": 127.63,
          "en": "So it's the first one in the array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.63,
          "end": 130.22,
          "en": "and we can do it as by reaching out to logMessages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.22,
          "end": 131.793,
          "en": "and using unshift.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.99,
          "end": 135.43,
          "en": "Unshift is basically like push,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.43,
          "end": 139.978,
          "en": "but where push adds something at the end of the array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.978,
          "end": 143.803,
          "en": "unshift adds something at the beginning of the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 148.73,
          "en": "And now it's up to you how a log message should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.73,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "Thus far in the course in the other lectures and modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 156.66,
          "en": "When we worked with lists and arrays and v-for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.66,
          "end": 161.14,
          "en": "we always had arrays full of strings full of text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.14,
          "end": 165.15,
          "en": "Here since we have free pieces of information that matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.15,
          "end": 168.62,
          "en": "I will actually add an object to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.62,
          "end": 171.22,
          "en": "So a log message is an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.22,
          "end": 174.05,
          "en": "and you will see how we can output does on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.05,
          "end": 175.95,
          "en": "in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.95,
          "end": 180.39,
          "en": "So here I will now add different pieces of information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.39,
          "end": 183.85,
          "en": "to this object to who, what and value to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.85,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "and I'll name the key actionBy: who",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 190.69,
          "en": "actionType: what",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.69,
          "end": 194.59,
          "en": "and actionValue the value we got.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.59,
          "end": 197.73,
          "en": "So we add an object to our logMessages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.73,
          "end": 201.94,
          "en": "which has three keys action by action type and action value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.94,
          "end": 204.24,
          "en": "So that we know who did the action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.24,
          "end": 205.9,
          "en": "which kind of action it was",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.9,
          "end": 207.963,
          "en": "and what the value of the action was.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.36,
          "end": 211.93,
          "en": "That's how we add logMessages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.93,
          "end": 214.7,
          "en": "And now a new log message should be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.7,
          "end": 218.12,
          "en": "when we for example, attack the monster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.12,
          "end": 222.75,
          "en": "So here in attackMonster, before the monster attacks us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.75,
          "end": 227.75,
          "en": "I want to call addLogMessage, so this newly added method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 227.86,
          "end": 230.37,
          "en": "and set to who to player",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.37,
          "end": 233.4,
          "en": "because the player attacked the monster",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.4,
          "end": 236.73,
          "en": "wants to set the action to attack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.73,
          "end": 241.73,
          "en": "and pass in the attackValue like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.53,
          "end": 247.05,
          "en": "Now, when the monster attacks us here in attackPlayer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 247.05,
          "end": 249.11,
          "en": "I also want to add a log message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.11,
          "end": 252.26,
          "en": "but now it's the monster who attacked us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.26,
          "end": 256.223,
          "en": "for this given attack value, which you derive here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 257.35,
          "end": 260.65,
          "en": "Of course, we do the same for the special attack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.65,
          "end": 263.37,
          "en": "Here the player attacks the monster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.37,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "We could also name this special-attack,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.03,
          "en": "but that's really up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.03,
          "end": 271.25,
          "en": "how you wanna handle those different types later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.25,
          "end": 272.77,
          "en": "I will not differentiate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.77,
          "end": 275.19,
          "en": "between special attack and regular attack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 275.19,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "So I will just name it, attack here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 280.77,
          "en": "If you would want to add such a differentiation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 280.77,
          "end": 283.64,
          "en": "you could use a different identifier here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 283.64,
          "end": 285.003,
          "en": "but I'll stick to attack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 286.81,
          "end": 288.89,
          "en": "Last but not least for healing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 288.89,
          "end": 293.89,
          "en": "the player heals himself for the heel value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 294.58,
          "end": 297.603,
          "en": "So that is the log message I wanna add here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 299.73,
          "end": 303.32,
          "en": "So now we've got these different logMessages being added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.32,
          "end": 306.4,
          "en": "with that our logMessages array will grow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.4,
          "end": 310.223,
          "en": "And now the question is how we output those messages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.34,
          "end": 315.06,
          "en": "In index.html we got this unordered list here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.06,
          "end": 316.47,
          "en": "in our battle log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.47,
          "end": 318.74,
          "en": "and this unordered list should render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 318.74,
          "end": 321.04,
          "en": "a bunch of lists items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.04,
          "end": 322.43,
          "en": "As I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 322.43,
          "end": 326.503,
          "en": "you don't need to use a list item to use v-for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.503,
          "end": 329.21,
          "en": "V-for can be used on any element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 329.21,
          "end": 331.41,
          "en": "but since we're outputting lists of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 331.41,
          "end": 334.45,
          "en": "and we want to write semantically correct code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 334.45,
          "end": 337.72,
          "en": "often you will use v-for on list items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.72,
          "end": 341.63,
          "en": "because that is the semantically correct HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 341.63,
          "end": 343.40999999999997,
          "en": "well for list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 343.40999999999997,
          "end": 345.17,
          "en": "That's just a side note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 345.17,
          "end": 347.25,
          "en": "The more important thing of course here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.25,
          "end": 349.1,
          "en": "that we use v-for though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 349.1,
          "end": 351.68,
          "en": "a nice Vue directive we learned about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 351.68,
          "end": 355,
          "en": "which can help us with outputting a list content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 355,
          "end": 358.19,
          "en": "It allows us to repeat this list item element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 358.19,
          "end": 360.75,
          "en": "and create it as often as needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 360.75,
          "end": 364.571,
          "en": "to have one list item HTML element on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 364.571,
          "end": 369.43,
          "en": "per item in our logMessages array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 369.43,
          "end": 372.43,
          "en": "So therefore here we need to refer to logMessages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 372.43,
          "end": 375.32,
          "en": "and go through it with the in key word",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 375.32,
          "end": 378.97,
          "en": "and then get access to every single log message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 378.97,
          "end": 381.89,
          "en": "which we now can use on an inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 381.89,
          "end": 384.363,
          "en": "of this repeated list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 387.08,
          "end": 388.053,
          "en": "And now here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 389.24,
          "end": 390.88,
          "en": "The content we want to output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 390.88,
          "end": 393.44,
          "en": "of course is fully up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 393.44,
          "end": 395.9,
          "en": "We could use interpolation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 395.9,
          "end": 399.69,
          "en": "to output the action by field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 399.69,
          "end": 403.15999999999997,
          "en": "which is one of the free fields we add as a log message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 403.15999999999997,
          "end": 405.747,
          "en": "which basically indicates who did something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 405.747,
          "end": 408.39,
          "en": "Then we could add a dash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 408.39,
          "end": 410.96,
          "en": "and a new piece of interpolation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 410.96,
          "end": 413.513,
          "en": "to output logMessage.actionType",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 417.223,
